WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.090
When a fuel burns, the bonds
in its molecules are broken.

2
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:07.090
And breaking a bond
always takes energy in.

3
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.290
It never gives energy out.

4
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:13.950
Yet a burning fuel gives out a great
deal of energy, as heat and light.

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.290
If breaking bonds takes in energy, how
can burning a fuel give energy out?

6
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.710
In this mission, you'll
meet bond enthalpy,

7
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.570
and use data-booklet values to estimate
the enthalpy change of a reaction.

8
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.910
You'll count the bonds
broken and the bonds made,

9
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:32.710
and find out why the
answer is only an estimate.

10
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:36.910
Your mission: explain how burning
a fuel can give energy out.
